<title>USA: AEP 1,090 MW Cook 2 nuclear unit at 55 pct.</title>
<headline>AEP 1,090 MW Cook 2 nuclear unit at 55 pct.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Electric Power Co's 1,090 megawatt (MW) Cook 2 nuclear power unit in Bridgman, Mich., is holding at 55 percent power for repairs, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said Thursday.</p>
<p>The unit is operating at this power level &quot;to repair both electronic feedwater pump controllers,&quot; the NRC said in its morning plant status report.</p>
<p>The adjacent unit, with a generating capacity of 1,020 MW, is operating at 94 percent power.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +212-859-1628))</p>
</text>
